---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About briomar"
	description="Systems, Mobile & Performance Engineering"
	pubDate={new Date('October 09 2026')}
>
	<p>
		Welcome to <strong>briomar</strong>, an independent engineering publication focused on Android systems architecture, mobile performance optimization, and resilient offline tools for emerging markets.
	</p>

	<p>
		The investigations published here take an empirical, evidence-first approach to analyzing production mobile software: decompiling client binaries, inspecting execution lifecycles, and profiling thread bottlenecks using modern engineering tools.
	</p>

	<h3>Core Technical Focus</h3>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Mobile & Systems:</strong> Android SDK (Jetpack Compose, Telephony, USSD, Room, IPC), Kotlin, Java</li>
		<li><strong>Performance & Forensics:</strong> JADX, APKTool, Perfetto, Systrace, Bytecode Analysis</li>
		<li><strong>Backend & Architecture:</strong> Offline-First Protocols, High-Throughput Services, GSM/Telephony Protocol Formulation</li>
		<li><strong>Web:</strong> Astro, TypeScript, Next.js, Modern Edge Deployments</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>What You'll Find On This Site</h3>
	<p>
		Detailed architectural teardowns of widely used consumer mobile applications, deep-dives into mobile runtime performance bottlenecks, and companion proof-of-concept prototypes that demonstrate faster, more resilient alternatives.
	</p>

	<h3>Feedback & Discussion</h3>
	<p>
		Have technical feedback, alternative benchmarks, or thoughts on any teardown? Join the discussion directly in the peer-review comment module at the bottom of each article.
	</p>
</Layout>
